      "content": "1.1 Location & Basic Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The territory is divided into three distinct physical zones: Jammu Region, Kashmir Valley, and Ladakh Region.",
        "Drainage is dominated by the Indus River System, the Jhelum River System, and the rivers of the Jammu Region.",
        "Topography and accessibility are largely defined by prominent mountain ranges, high-altitude passes, and glaciers.",
        "The region supports varied ecosystems, spanning sub-tropical forests to high-altitude cold desert sanctuaries."
      ],
      "id": "nbteih2"
    },
