    {
      "id": "dp4zh1r",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.2 Physical Divisions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "joxhtr9",
      "content": "Jammu &amp; Kashmir is broadly divided into THREE distinct physiographic regions:"
    },
    {
      "id": "937hfak",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "A. Jammu Region"
    },
    {
      "id": "av4f7t2",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Located in the southernmost part; sub-tropical &amp; semi-arid plains",
        "Sub-Himalayan foothills (Shivaliks) — elevations between 300–1200 m",
        "Important plains: Jammu, Kathua, Samba, Udhampur, Reasi",
        "Tawi, Devika, Ujh, Basantar are key rivers",
        "Famous for: Vaishno Devi shrine, Bahu Fort, Surinsar-Mansar lakes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "vdh55hb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "B. Kashmir Valley"
    },
    {
      "id": "eovf9i3",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "A high-altitude valley at ~1,600 m above sea level",
        "Surrounded by Pir Panjal in south and Greater Himalayas in north",
        "Length ~135 km; width ~32–40 km",
        "Drained by the Jhelum River",
        "Fertile alluvial soil — called 'Paradise on Earth'",
        "Famous: Dal Lake, Wular Lake, Nagin Lake, Srinagar, Gulmarg, Pahalgam, Sonamarg"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ibfxd7y",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "C. Ladakh Region"
    },
    {
      "id": "73ztrj1",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Trans-Himalayan cold desert plateau — avg elevation 3,000–5,000 m",
        "Highest motorable road: Umling La (19,024 ft / 5,883 m) in Ladakh",
        "Indus, Shyok, Zanskar rivers drain the region",
        "Famous: Pangong Tso, Tso Moriri, Nubra Valley, Zanskar Valley, Siachen",
        "World's highest battlefield: Siachen Glacier (~6,400 m)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "v6nmi4u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.3 Mountain Ranges"
    },
    {
      "id": "y8ldxty",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Range</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Features</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Karakoram Range</strong></p>",
            "<p>Northernmost; contains K2 (8,611 m) — 2nd highest peak in world; Siachen Glacier</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Greater Himalayas (Himadri)</strong></p>",
            "<p>Contains Nun (7,135 m) — highest peak in J&amp;K; Zoji La pass</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Pir Panjal Range</strong></p>",
            "<p>Separates Kashmir Valley from Jammu; Banihal Pass, Pir Ki Gali</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Zanskar Range</strong></p>",
            "<p>Between Kashmir &amp; Ladakh; Pensi La pass</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Ladakh Range</strong></p>",
            "<p>Separates Indus and Shyok valleys in Ladakh</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
