        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Lipulekh Pass</strong></p>",
            "<p>5,334 m; tri-junction of India, China, Nepal</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "slhip48",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.5 Rivers of J&K"
    },
    {
      "id": "gy9bwlm",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Indus River System"
    },
    {
      "id": "25l9kap",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Indus: Originates from Tibetan plateau near Mansarovar; flows through Ladakh; basin covers most of Ladakh",
        "Shyok: Tributary of Indus; flows through Nubra Valley",
        "Zanskar: Joins Indus near Nimmu; famous for Chadar Trek (frozen river)",
        "Suru: Flows from Nun-Kun massif; joins Indus at Kargil"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "8mhcp5f",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Jhelum River System"
    },
    {
      "id": "jpugjtt",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Jhelum (Vitasta in ancient times): Originates from Verinag spring (Anantnag); flows through Srinagar → Wular Lake → Baramulla → Pakistan",
        "Length in J&amp;K: ~175 km; perennial river",
        "Liddar: Flows from Kolahoi glacier; joins Jhelum at Bijbehara",
        "Vishav: Joins Jhelum; originates from Pir Panjal glaciers",
        "Bring / Romushi / Pohru: Minor tributaries of Jhelum"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "78gptve",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Rivers of Jammu Region"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1g6c1n",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Chenab (Chandrabhaga): Enters J&amp;K from HP; Baglihar Dam built on it",
        "Tawi: Flows through Jammu city; tributary of Chenab",
        "Ravi: Flows through Chamba before entering Pakistan; Ranjit Sagar Dam",
        "Ujh: Flows through Kathua; joins Ravi"
      ]
    },
    {
